# Claude Design (manual export consumer)

Authoritative knowledge for the `ux-agent` when the project's design integration is **claude-design**. Claude Design (`https://claude.ai/design`) has **no MCP, no public API**. The handoff is **always manual**: designer produces mockups in the web app, exports them locally, drops them under `docs/design/<EPIC-SEQ>/`. This skill ingests the bundle and writes `DESIGN.md`.

The ux-agent loads this skill and follows it step by step.

---

## Inputs

| Path | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `docs/design/<EPIC-SEQ>/` | **User-exported bundle** — screens, tokens, components inventory (see Bundle layout below) |
| `docs/design/schema.json` | Workspace pointer — `designSystem.url` (claude.ai/design link), accumulated `tokens.*` |
| `docs/features/<id>/REQUIREMENTS.md` § Screen inventory | Authoritative screen list (coverage check) |
| `CLAUDE.md` + `<framework>-patterns/SKILL.md` per declared stack | Form-factor mapping |

## Outputs

| File | Mutation |
|---|---|
| `docs/features/<id>/DESIGN.md` | **Created / replaced** — screens table referencing exports, tokens table, implementation notes |
| `docs/features/<id>/REQUIREMENTS.md` § Visual spec | One-line link to DESIGN.md |
| `docs/design/schema.json` | `tokens.*` arrays extended from extracted CSS vars / Tailwind classes (dedup by name+value) |
| `docs/features/<id>/state.json` | `design = complete`, `design_artifact = "docs/features/<id>/DESIGN.md"`, `design_provider = "claude-design"` |

The ux-agent does NOT modify exports under `docs/design/<id>/` — user-owned, read-only.

---

## Bundle layout — what the user exports

```
docs/design/<EPIC-SEQ>/
├── README.md                           # which claude.ai/design page(s) sourced (optional)
├── screens/
│   ├── <screen>-<form-factor>.html     # preferred — preserves layout + tokens
│   ├── <screen>-<form-factor>.png      # alternative — image only
│   └── ...
├── tokens.css                          # OR tokens.json — exported design tokens
└── components.md                       # component inventory + usage notes (optional)
```

Filename convention: `<screen-name>-<form-factor>.<ext>`. Form factors match Phase 2 below (`mobile` / `tablet` / `desktop` / `responsive`). Example: `bookmark-list-mobile.html`, `bookmark-list-desktop.html`.

If the bundle is missing or empty, the ux-agent **escalates** — see Escalation below. Never invents content.

---

## Phase 1 — Locate the bundle

```
bundle_dir = docs/design/<EPIC-SEQ>/
if not exists(bundle_dir) OR empty(bundle_dir):
  emit [NEEDS CLARIFICATION] (see Escalation)
  design = pending in docs/features/<id>/state.json
  abort — do NOT proceed
```

---

## Phase 2 — Form-factor mapping

Same rule as figma — requirements-first. These are the form factors whose exports are *required*; **never demand an export for device support the requirements don't state**. Decide in order; first match wins:

1. **Team convention** — `<framework>-patterns/SKILL.md § Design system + visual conventions` specifies form factors → use those.
2. **Requirements** — `REQUIREMENTS.md` / PRD / story (incl. NFRs) mention responsive, mobile, tablet, breakpoints, or device support → exactly the named form factors: `mobile` (375w), `tablet` (768w), `desktop` (1440w) as applicable.
3. **Stack's native surface, single form factor** — web stack → `desktop` (1440w) only; mobile stack → `mobile` (375w) only. Extra exports the designer dropped beyond the required set are linked, not escalated.
4. **No frontend / mobile stack declared** — skip; emit `[NEEDS CLARIFICATION]` asking which form factors to design.

---

## Phase 3 — Enumerate screens

Walk `docs/design/<id>/screens/`. Parse filenames:

```
For each file matching <name>-<form-factor>.(html|png|svg):
  enumerate as (screen=<name>, form_factor=<form-factor>, ext=<ext>, path=<rel-path>)
```

Group by screen → set of form factors covered.

### Coverage check

Cross-reference against `REQUIREMENTS.md § Screen inventory` AND Phase 2 form factors:

```
For each (screen, form_factor) the inventory requires:
  if missing from bundle → escalate with [NEEDS CLARIFICATION]
For each screen in bundle not in inventory:
  warn (don't block) — extra screen, may be intentional
```

---

## Phase 4 — Token extraction

### From `tokens.css` (CSS custom properties)

```
:root {
  --color-primary: #1A73E8;
  --color-bg-surface: #FFFFFF;
  --spacing-md: 16px;
  --text-body-size: 14px;
  --text-body-line-height: 20px;
}
```

Parse to `{ name, value, kind }`. Classify by name prefix:
- `--color-*`, `--bg-*`, `--text-*-color`, `--border-*` → `tokens.color`
- `--spacing-*`, `--gap-*`, `--padding-*`, `--radius-*` → `tokens.spacing`
- `--text-*-size`, `--text-*-line-height`, `--font-*` → `tokens.typography`

### From `tokens.json`

```jsonc
{
  "color":      { "primary": "#1A73E8", "bg-surface": "#FFFFFF" },
  "spacing":    { "md": 16, "lg": 24 },
  "typography": { "body": { "size": 14, "line-height": 20, "weight": 400 } }
}
```

Flatten to the same `{ name, value, kind }` shape.

### From HTML exports (when no `tokens.css` / `tokens.json` present)

Fallback — parse `<style>` blocks of `screens/*.html`. Look for:
- `:root { --... }` declarations
- Tailwind utility classes if no CSS vars present (then escalate — Tailwind class extraction is heuristic, not authoritative)

### Append to workspace store

Update `docs/design/schema.json` `tokens.{color,spacing,typography}` arrays. Dedup by `name` (first occurrence wins; warn on value conflicts).

---

## Phase 5 — Component extraction (optional)

If `components.md` exists in the bundle, parse it as a flat list:

```markdown
# Components used (<EPIC-SEQ>)

- **Button** — primary CTA across all screens; uses --color-primary
- **Input** — text fields on edit screens; uses --color-bg-surface
- ...
```

If absent, extract `data-component="<name>"` attributes from HTML exports as a best-effort inventory. Document the extraction method in DESIGN.md.

---

## Phase 6 — Write-back

### 6a. DESIGN.md (per feature) — created / replaced wholesale

Location: `docs/features/<EPIC-SEQ>/DESIGN.md`.

```markdown
# Design — <EPIC-SEQ> <Feature title>

**Provider:** claude-design (manual export)
**Source page:** <claude.ai/design URL from schema.json designSystem.url, OR docs/design/<id>/README.md, OR "user-supplied — see bundle">
**Bundle:** [docs/design/<EPIC-SEQ>/](../../design/<EPIC-SEQ>/)
**Generated:** <ISO8601> by ux-agent

## Screens × form factors

| Screen | <FormFactor1> | <FormFactor2> | Components used |
|---|---|---|---|
| <Screen> | [<form1>.html](../../design/<id>/screens/<screen>-<form1>.html) | [<form2>.html](../../design/<id>/screens/<screen>-<form2>.html) | <list> |

## Tokens used (this feature)
- Color: <list of token names extracted in Phase 4>
- Spacing: <list>
- Typography: <list>

## Implementation notes for /arh-implement
- Token values live at `docs/design/<id>/tokens.{css,json}` and in workspace `docs/design/schema.json`
- Components consumed via `<framework>-patterns` mapping — engineers translate `--color-primary` etc. to the project's CSS/Tailwind/styled system
- Form-factor breakpoints: <list with widths>
- Component inventory: <list from Phase 5>

## Source bundle
- Exports under `docs/design/<id>/screens/` — user-owned, do not modify
- Tokens at `docs/design/<id>/tokens.{css,json}`
- Component notes (if present) at `docs/design/<id>/components.md`
```

### 6b. REQUIREMENTS.md § Visual spec — one-line pointer

Locate the `## Visual spec` heading. Replace ONLY its body. Other sections untouched.

```markdown
## Visual spec

See [DESIGN.md](./DESIGN.md) — produced by `ux-agent` (claude-design provider) on <ISO8601 date>.
```

### 6c. schema.json — accumulate tokens

```jsonc
{
  "tokens": {
    "color":      [],
    "spacing":    [],
    "typography": []
  }
}
```

### 6d. Per-feature state

Set on `docs/features/<EPIC-SEQ>/state.json` (mirror `design` to the index — B-tier):

```json
{
  "design":          "complete",
  "design_artifact": "docs/features/<EPIC-SEQ>/DESIGN.md",
  "design_provider": "claude-design"
}
```

