## Escalation patterns

Emit a `[NEEDS CLARIFICATION]` block in DESIGN.md AND set `design = pending` (NOT `complete`) in `docs/features/<id>/state.json` when:

- `docs/design/<EPIC-SEQ>/` missing or empty
- A screen in `REQUIREMENTS.md § Screen inventory` has no export for one or more required form factors
- `tokens.css` / `tokens.json` missing AND HTML exports yield no extractable token sets
- Bundle contains screens NOT in REQUIREMENTS.md § Screen inventory (warn, don't block)

Marker format:

```markdown
## [NEEDS CLARIFICATION]

- **Blocker:** <one-line — e.g. "bundle missing", "screen X has no mobile export", "no token export found">
- **What's needed:** <specific action — e.g. "Export 'BookmarkList' for mobile (375w) and drop into docs/design/<id>/screens/">
- **Where:** <expected path / source page URL>
```

---

## Anti-patterns

- Fetching claude.ai/design URLs programmatically — no API; URL is reference only.
- Modifying files under `docs/design/<id>/screens/` — user-owned exports are read-only.
- Inventing token values — extract from `tokens.css` / `tokens.json` / `<style>` blocks ONLY.
- Inventing screen names — `REQUIREMENTS.md § Screen inventory` is authoritative.
- Embedding PNG screenshots inline in DESIGN.md — link to the export file under `docs/design/<id>/screens/` instead.
- Writing to `REQUIREMENTS.md` sections other than `## Visual spec`.

---

## Storage convention recap

```
docs/design/
├── schema.json                         # workspace pointer + accumulated tokens
└── <EPIC-SEQ>/                         # per-feature export bundle (user-owned)
    ├── README.md                       # optional — which claude.ai/design page(s)
    ├── screens/<name>-<form>.html|png  # exports
    ├── tokens.css|tokens.json          # extracted design tokens
    └── components.md                   # optional component inventory

docs/features/<EPIC-SEQ>/
└── DESIGN.md                           # produced by ux-agent — links to bundle
```

